  "steps": [
    "In a bowl, combine the pork, green onions, ginger, garlic, oyster sauce, pepper, chili crisp, soy sauce, sesame oil and rice vinegar. Mix until fully combined.",
    "Set a bowl of water next to an 8-inch round or square heatproof baking dish (it must fit inside your pot if you are steaming).",
    "Dip each wrapper in the water and layer like lasagna: a layer of overlapping wrappers, a thin layer of pork, then repeat until everything is used, ending with wrappers.",
    "Pour the broth evenly over the top.",
    "To steam: bring 1 to 2 inches of water to a boil in a large pot, set the dish inside on a rack, cover, and steam 20-23 minutes, until the pork in the center reads 160°F.",
    "To bake instead: heat the oven to 375°F. Set the dish in a larger pan of hot water, cover tightly with foil, and bake 30-35 minutes, until the center reads 160°F.",
    "Top with soy sauce, chili crisp, green onion and sesame seeds, and serve."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Keep each pork layer thin so the center cooks through at the same time as the edges."
  ],
